            "datePublished": "2026-06-27",
            "description": "Cross-discipline reuse: the Galaxy Training Network 'Introduction to image analysis' workflow (threshold, label, count, measure), built to count cell nuclei, applied unchanged to a Sentinel-2 chip of the Greenland ice sheet to detect and measure supraglacial melt ponds, and benchmarked against independent lake outlines (Glen et al.). The data are GeoTIFF/TIFF where the Earth-observation FIP declares NetCDF: the bioimaging workflow only accepts image formats, a deviation caused by the cross-domain reuse itself.",
